Same maze, same generate() in prepare. The reference's visited grid, path Vec and queue are arrays (262,144 slots for the path and queue; the search discovers 185,157 cells for the run parameters, measured by simulating it); the per-run visited array is a fill. The reference materialises the path as a Vec and reverses it; here the length and the middle cell are taken from the chain of parents, the same information the checksum uses. Other stores are range-checked; state is unlogged, so nothing is saved for a rollback. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: visited, py, px, pp, q) is not logged (state is unlogged by default, so no undo log, as a Rust local has none).
